WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:03.030
- All right y'all, the hours
almost up, but not quite yet.

00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:05.310
Let's check out something
that's sure to make you smile.

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:06.359
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:06.359 --> 00:00:08.942
(upbeat music)

00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:12.260
When a Florida special
ed teacher realized most

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:15.020
of the students at her
school had never seen snow.

00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:17.080
She came up with a very
cool way to give them an

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:19.070
up close and personal experience.

00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:20.720
She called her sister in Kentucky.

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:24.200
Asked her to build a snowman
and ship it to her class.

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:25.570
Low it the what?

00:00:25.570 --> 00:00:26.500
That's crazy.

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:28.040
Like, how do you do that?

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:31.915
Low and behold, Lucky the
Snowman made the 800 mile journey

00:00:31.915 --> 00:00:35.268
to the total delight of her students.

00:00:35.268 --> 00:00:37.064
- Aww are you serious?

00:00:37.064 --> 00:00:38.380
(teacher gasping)

00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:39.424
- He made it.

00:00:39.424 --> 00:00:41.431
- (Guest) He made it.

00:00:41.431 --> 00:00:42.264
- He made it.

00:00:42.264 --> 00:00:43.534
(teacher clapping)

00:00:43.534 --> 00:00:44.367
He made it.

00:00:44.367 --> 00:00:45.200
(crowd clapping)

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:46.033
- Aww.

00:00:46.033 --> 00:00:48.610
- We have this remarkable
teacher, Robin and her sister

00:00:48.610 --> 00:00:50.100
Amber on the line right now.

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:51.086
What's up ladies?

00:00:51.086 --> 00:00:52.664
(crowd cheering)

00:00:52.664 --> 00:00:54.620
- Hi Kelly.
- Hi Kelly.

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:57.590
First of all, Amber, like
what did you think when

00:00:57.590 --> 00:01:00.030
Robin asked you to build
and ship a snowman?

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:02.910
I don't think that's
ever been asked, ever.

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:05.350
- Well, when my sister
puts me up for a challenge

00:01:05.350 --> 00:01:07.096
I don't back down at all.

00:01:07.096 --> 00:01:10.310
So never in a million years did I think

00:01:10.310 --> 00:01:12.780
that we would have such a perfect snow to

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:14.610
build such a perfect little snowman.

00:01:14.610 --> 00:01:16.100
But on January 8th,

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:18.388
we had snow that equaled about 10 inches.

00:01:18.388 --> 00:01:19.221
- Wow.

00:01:19.221 --> 00:01:21.470
- So, out I went to build a snowman.

00:01:21.470 --> 00:01:22.810
So, I put him together.

00:01:22.810 --> 00:01:25.020
He was about 18 inches tall.

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:28.693
Complete with blueberry
eyes, blueberry buttons for,

00:01:28.693 --> 00:01:30.400
for his shirt.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:32.410
And I also put little sticks

00:01:32.410 --> 00:01:33.540
for his arms -
- (audience awing)

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:35.360
and his carrot nose.

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:39.120
I brought out a box and
it was lined in styrofoam

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:41.610
and took lots and lots of ice packs,

00:01:41.610 --> 00:01:44.760
put him inside there, packaged
him up and sent him down

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:46.170
to the shipping station.

00:01:46.170 --> 00:01:47.980
And believe it or not -
- He made it. He made it.

00:01:47.980 --> 00:01:51.290
when I shipped him out, a piece
of my heart, went with him.

00:01:51.290 --> 00:01:53.490
I felt connected to this little guy.

00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:54.780
So off he went -
- Aww.

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:56.950
and I caught myself
being up all night long

00:01:56.950 --> 00:01:59.193
tracking to watch to make
sure he made it Tampa.

00:01:59.193 --> 00:02:00.370
(Kelly laughing)

00:02:00.370 --> 00:02:01.479
- That's awesome.

00:02:01.479 --> 00:02:02.490
(audience clapping)

00:02:02.490 --> 00:02:04.730
So Robin, were you worried

00:02:04.730 --> 00:02:07.570
that he'd be melted by the
time you opened the box?

00:02:07.570 --> 00:02:12.330
- Listen, when I got that
box, it was like Fort Knox.

00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:16.100
He was taped up like Fort Knox,
but I could feel, my heart

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:19.120
was just pounding and I
could feel him actually.

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:20.131
He was cold.

00:02:20.131 --> 00:02:23.590
So, I opened it up and I peeled
it back and there he was.

00:02:23.590 --> 00:02:24.770
He was perfect.

00:02:24.770 --> 00:02:27.212
So I rushed him down to the
classroom so that the kids

00:02:27.212 --> 00:02:30.130
could see him and they were so excited.

00:02:30.130 --> 00:02:31.750
So, he's excited to meet you.

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:33.743
So here he is, he's doing great.

00:02:33.743 --> 00:02:34.733
The kids -
- Oh my gosh.

00:02:34.733 --> 00:02:35.566
just love him Kelly.

00:02:35.566 --> 00:02:36.399
(audience clapping)

00:02:36.399 --> 00:02:38.770
- I go in, they're so excited to see him

00:02:38.770 --> 00:02:39.940
and he's brought such joy

00:02:39.940 --> 00:02:41.060
to our school.

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:42.191
And we're just so happy.

00:02:42.191 --> 00:02:44.270
They wanna, you know, I
take him outta the lot

00:02:44.270 --> 00:02:46.620
of the times the kids wanna
wave at him and they wanna know

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:48.572
if he's like Olaf, is
he gonna come to life?

00:02:48.572 --> 00:02:49.681
(audience chattering)

00:02:49.681 --> 00:02:50.810
But, he has brought such joy.

00:02:50.810 --> 00:02:53.070
And I, I can't tell you
the joy that he's brought

00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:54.570
to us here at our school.

00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:56.650
And you know, when I think
about him, I get a little

00:02:56.650 --> 00:02:57.860
I get a little emotional.

00:02:57.860 --> 00:02:58.693
I'm not gonna lie.

00:02:58.693 --> 00:03:00.601
I get emotional when I think about him.

00:03:00.601 --> 00:03:01.810
- Aw, that's so sweet.

00:03:01.810 --> 00:03:02.643
It is magical.

00:03:02.643 --> 00:03:03.700
I remember the first one made a snowman

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:05.560
with my kids and they
really hadn't been in snow.

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:06.870
It's a magical little moment.

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:08.850
So that's really cool that
you did that for your kids.

00:03:08.850 --> 00:03:10.360
Thank you so much, Robin.

00:03:10.360 --> 00:03:12.360
Thank you, Amber.

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:14.593
I'm liking your post right now.

00:03:16.150 --> 00:03:17.590
And that's not all ladies

00:03:17.590 --> 00:03:19.233
our season long partner Pilot Pen Makers.

00:03:19.233 --> 00:03:20.572
A Frixion that go to a erasable pen

00:03:20.572 --> 00:03:22.183
of the Kelly Clarkson Show,

00:03:22.183 --> 00:03:25.530
want to celebrate those creating
fearlessly just like y'all.

00:03:25.530 --> 00:03:27.140
So they're gonna give
you a thousand dollars.

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:28.753
That's $500 each.

00:03:28.753 --> 00:03:31.836
(audience cheering)

00:03:33.450 --> 00:03:34.630
Thank you so much.

00:03:34.630 --> 00:03:36.953
This is such a sweet
kind thing that you did.

